⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the exact-patch guard is keyed to a hard-coded 2-entry map — a future self-hosted leg silently escapes it**

The new gh-1826 guard iterates `const {build-mobile.yml: build-ios, build-macos.yml: build-macos}`. Today that covers every `setup-flutter-selfhosted` usage in the repo (verified: only `.github/workflows/build-macos.yml:301` and `.github/workflows/build-mobile.yml:799`), but nothing fails when a **third** self-hosted leg is added with a wildcard pin — the exact bug class this test exists to prevent walks straight past the guard.

The sibling guard in the same file already establishes the right pattern — it scans **all** workflow files dynamically and asserts a presence floor so a topology change can't silently shrink its coverage:

```dart
// test/setup_flutter_selfhosted_test.dart:422-492
final workflows = Directory('.github/workflows').listSync()...
expect(checked, greaterThanOrEqualTo(3),
    reason: '... the workflow topology changed and this guard scanned nothing');
```

Suggested shape (keeps the equal-`3.47.7` assertion for the two known lanes, adds the completeness floor):

```dart
const pinnedVersion = '3.47.7';
final usages = <String, String>{}; // file -> job, discovered by scanning
// every workflow's steps for `uses: ./.github/actions/setup-flutter-selfhosted`
expect(usages.keys, containsAll(const {
  '.github/workflows/build-mobile.yml',
  '.github/workflows/build-macos.yml',
}));
for (final entry in usages.entries) {
  // ... existing expect(version, pinnedVersion, reason: ...)
}
```

(An alternative that matches the test's own name even more literally: assert every discovered pin matches `RegExp(r'^\d+\.\d+\.\d+$')` — "exact patch, never a wildcard" — instead of equality with one const, so a conscious two-PR rolling bump of the lanes doesn't need a simultaneous edit here. Either closing the topology hole is the point.)

